---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Research & Documentation | Finicky Bee"
  description="Explore the Finicky Bee research and documentation process for vintage and antique collectibles, following physical evidence, historical sources, and documented context."
>
  <main>
        <Header />

    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="narrow">
        <p class="eyebrow">RESEARCH & DOCUMENTATION</p>

        <h1>Look closer. Follow the evidence.</h1>

        <p class="hero-text">
          A research approach built around observation, documented sources,
          careful comparison, and transparency about what is known and what
          remains uncertain.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="narrow">
        <p class="eyebrow">THE RESEARCH APPROACH</p>

        <h2>Every object begins with questions.</h2>

        <p>
          Research at Finicky Bee begins with the object itself. Physical
          characteristics, construction, materials, marks, labels, condition,
          and other observable details provide the starting point.
        </p>

        <p>
          From there, available evidence is examined alongside documented
          sources, maker information, historical references, and comparable
          examples when appropriate.
        </p>

        <p>
          The purpose is not simply to arrive at a name or date. It is to build
          a documented understanding of what the available evidence can
          reasonably support.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section research-principles">
      <div class="narrow">
        <p class="eyebrow">WHAT WE EXAMINE</p>

        <h2>Evidence can come from many places.</h2>

        <div class="principle-list">
          <article>
            <span>01</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Physical Evidence</h3>
              <p>
                Shape, construction, dimensions, materials, surface details,
                condition, and other observable characteristics.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span>02</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Marks & Labels</h3>
              <p>
                Signatures, maker's marks, manufacturer's marks, labels,
                stamps, inscriptions, and other identifying details.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span>03</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Documented Sources</h3>
              <p>
                Books, catalogs, historical records, manufacturer information,
                institutional resources, and other relevant references.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span>04</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Comparative Evidence</h3>
              <p>
                Comparable examples may help establish patterns in design,
                construction, materials, markings, or production.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span>05</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Context</h3>
              <p>
                Historical, cultural, geographic, manufacturing, and collecting
                context can help explain where an object fits within its story.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section evidence">
      <div class="narrow">
        <p class="eyebrow">EVIDENCE BEFORE ASSUMPTION</p>

        <h2>What can be supported matters.</h2>

        <p>
          Research sometimes produces a clear identification. Other times, the
          available evidence supports only a broader conclusion.
        </p>

        <p>
          Finicky Bee distinguishes between documented information,
          observations made directly from an object, reasonable research
          conclusions, and information that remains uncertain.
        </p>

        <p>
          When evidence is incomplete or conflicting, that uncertainty is
          preserved rather than replaced with unsupported certainty.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section uncertainty">
      <div class="narrow">
        <p class="eyebrow">WHEN THE ANSWER IS UNCERTAIN</p>

        <h2>Uncertainty is part of responsible research.</h2>

        <p>
          Not every collectible comes with a complete history. Marks may be
          worn away, records may be unavailable, sources may disagree, or an
          object's original context may have been lost over time.
        </p>

        <p>
          In those situations, Finicky Bee documents what can be established
          and clearly identifies what remains unknown or unresolved.
        </p>

        <p>
          An unanswered question is still useful when it is preserved honestly
          for future research.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section research-record">
      <div class="narrow">
        <p class="eyebrow">FROM RESEARCH TO RECORD</p>

        <h2>Research becomes part of an object's history.</h2>

        <p>
          Research findings, physical observations, photographs, and supporting
          information can become part of a lasting record connected to the
          object.
        </p>

        <p>
          This documentation helps preserve not only what was discovered, but
          also how that understanding was reached.
        </p>

        <a href="/collection" class="text-link">
          Explore the Collection →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section finds-link">
      <div class="narrow">
        <p class="eyebrow">SEE THE PROCESS IN ACTION</p>

        <h2>Follow a discovery from find to documented story.</h2>

        <p>
          Finicky Bee Finds explores selected objects through discovery,
          observation, research, documentation, and storytelling.
        </p>

        <a href="/finds" class="text-link">
          Explore Finicky Bee Finds →
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section founder">
      <div class="narrow">
        <p class="eyebrow">INDEPENDENT RESEARCH</p>

        <h2>Curiosity, documentation, and responsible collecting.</h2>

        <p>
          Finicky Bee is an independent collecting and research project.
          Research is conducted to better understand the objects within the
          collection and to preserve the information discovered about them.
        </p>

        <p>
          The work does not replace the expertise of qualified specialists,
          museums, archives, or other professional institutions when specialized
          expertise is required.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <div>
        <p class="footer-brand">FINICKY BEE</p>
        <p>Preserving Moments in Time — One Collectible at a Time.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="footer-links">
  <a href="/about">About</a>
  <a href="/finds">Finicky Bee Finds</a>
  <a href="/collection">Collection</a>
  <a href="/research">Research</a>
  <a href="/shop">Shop</a>
  <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
  <a href="/terms">Terms</a>
</div>

      <p class="copyright">
        © {new Date().getFullYear()} Finicky Bee. All rights reserved.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  :global(body) {
    margin: 0;
    background: #f7f3ea;
    color: #2f302c;
    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  }

    .footer-links a {
    color: #2f4f3f;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  .page-hero {
    padding: 110px 24px 90px;
    background: #2f4f3f;
    color: #f7f3ea;
  }

  .section {
    max-width: 1180px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 90px 24px;
  }

  .narrow {
    max-width: 780px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    color: #d4a437;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  h3 {
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.7rem, 6vw, 5rem);
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 28px;
    color: #2f4f3f;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.4rem);
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    color: #2f4f3f;
    font-size: 1.45rem;
  }

  p {
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .hero-text {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 28px 0 0;
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .research-principles {
    background: #ece7da;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .principle-list {
    max-width: 780px;
    margin: 45px auto 0;
  }

  .principle-list article {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 55px 1fr;
    gap: 24px;
    padding: 28px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #d4a437;
  }

  .principle-list article > span {
    color: #d4a437;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }

  .principle-list p {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .evidence {
    background: #f7f3ea;
  }

  .uncertainty {
    background: #ece7da;
  }

  .research-record {
    background: #f7f3ea;
  }

  .finds-link {
    background: #2f4f3f;
    color: #f7f3ea;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .finds-link h2 {
    color: #f7f3ea;
  }

  .finds-link .text-link {
    color: #f7f3ea;
  }

  .founder {
    padding-bottom: 110px;
  }

  .text-link {
    color: #2f4f3f;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .text-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .site-footer {
    background: #2f4f3f;
    color: #f7f3ea;
    padding: 55px 24px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.5fr 1fr;
    gap: 40px;
  }

  .site-footer p {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }

  .footer-brand {
    color: #d4a437;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  }

  .footer-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 16px 22px;
  }

  .footer-links a {
    color: #f7f3ea;
  }

  .copyright {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    padding-top: 25px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(247, 243, 234, 0.2);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

    @media (max-width: 700px) {

    .page-hero {
      padding: 80px 24px 70px;
    }

    .section {
      padding: 65px 24px;
    }

    .principle-list article {
      grid-template-columns: 42px 1fr;
      gap: 16px;
    }

    .site-footer {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .copyright {
      grid-column: auto;
    }
  }
</style>